{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-68934",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, consider the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ 64\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ \\frac{64}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{64} & = \\\\ \\frac{64\\times 3}{1\\times 64} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{64}\\times 3}{1\\times \\cancel{64}} & = \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)\\times ((-8)^{2}\\times \\frac{3}{64}) & = \\\\ (-3)\\times 3 & = \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
